          "after": "The extraction preserves shader strings, point identity/order, raw-coordinate ENU conversion, color/ground thresholds, depth/attribute order, callback buffer operations, cached matrix copying and caller-owned resize scheduling. It adds no requests, timers or render-frame work. Detach now addresses the viewer that accepted registration, so replacing/clearing the host viewer reference cannot target the wrong viewer. Normal same-view removal and warning behavior remain unchanged. The retained post-detach snapshot policy matches the old cached-renderer lifetime.\n\nThe owner deliberately retains the previous GL release list and lasso attribute/shader behavior; GPU policy changes remain separate from this structural move. Acquisition, map layers/applyEdits, cropping policy, calibration intent, lasso hit testing and auto-follow remain runtime-owned. Point-cloud map-layer ownership is completed in the next recorded increment below.\n\n### Affected files\n"
